  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14190611/assets/defe06c87cab8ef89d21ee2a7fbd790b0dd4563d05409e9336e5f9b249f42a20.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on the interval $[-6,4].$ The graph of $y={f}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown above. It consists of three line segments and the arc of a semicircle with radius $2.$ If $f(-3)=5,$ calculate $f(4).$\n\n$f(4)=$\n{{field-1}}",
